<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corcu Duibne</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corcu Duibne were an early medieval Irish population group of west Munster, settled on the Dingle and Iveragh peninsulas of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kerry">County Kerry</a>. Counted among the Érainn, they were later subject to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eoganachta">Eóganacht</a> kings of Iarmumu. Their territory holds one of the densest concentrations of ogham stones, many naming members of the group.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corcu-duibne.jpg" alt="Corcu Duibne" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jim · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dunbeg_Fort,_Dingle_Peninsula,_Kerry,_Ireland..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
